-- title:
--   Ordinary condition is preserved by base change along local homomorphisms
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ and $B$ be commutative local rings, let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring with algebra structures on both $A$ and $B$, and let $\varphi \colon A \to B$ be a ring homomorphism which is local (`IsLocalHom`). Let $\rho$ be a [`GaloisRepAdic A`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16), that is, a free finite $A$-module $V$ with $\operatorname{rank}_A V = 2$ together with a monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ (realised as the $\mathbb Q$-algebra automorphisms of `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`) to $\operatorname{End}_A V$ satisfying the adic continuity condition that for each $n$ some finite extension $L/\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ has the property that every $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise satisfies $\rho(\sigma)v - v \in \mathfrak m_A^n \cdot V$ for all $v$. Assume, for a natural number $p$ and a finite set $S$ of naturals, that $\rho$ satisfies [`GaloisRep.ordinaryCondition 𝒪 p S`](def/GaloisRep_LocalConditions.html#L28), i.e. the conjunction of: $p \in \mathfrak m_A$ and, whenever $\sigma$ raises all $p^n$-th roots of unity to the power $a$, $\det \rho(\sigma) - a$ lies in the ideal generated by $p^n$; for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $p$ there is an $A$-line $L \subseteq V$, spanned by the first member of some basis of $V$ indexed by `Fin 2`, stable under the decomposition subgroup of $P$, with $\rho(\sigma)v - v \in L$ for all $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup and all $v \in V$; and for each prime $q \notin S$, inertia at every valuation subring over $q$ acts trivially. Then the base change $\rho.\mathrm{baseChangeAlong}\,\varphi$, on $B \otimes_A V$ with $\sigma$ acting by the base change of $\rho(\sigma)$, again satisfies [`GaloisRep.ordinaryCondition 𝒪 p S`](def/GaloisRep_LocalConditions.html#L28).
--
--   This records that the ordinary local condition of type $S$ at $p$ behaves as a deformation condition in Mazur's sense: it is stable under extension of the coefficient ring along a local homomorphism, which is what allows it to cut out a subfunctor of the deformation functor. It is used when ordinary deformation data are transported to quotients and to Hecke algebras, in the construction of patching data for the modularity lifting arguments.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_GaloisRepAdic_ordinaryCondition_baseChangeAlong.lean

import Definitions.Def_GaloisRep_LocalConditions

